Everything here is the authors' own work and carries no copyleft dependency.
MIT is used for the code rather than a Creative Commons licence, which Creative
Commons itself discourages for software; CC-BY-4.0 is used for the dataset,
where attribution is the point.

The electrode detector and its training code are NOT part of this repository.
They build on Ultralytics YOLO (AGPL-3.0) and are not required to reproduce any
result in the clinical paper. See the paper's data and code availability
statement.

